WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
(crowd cheering)

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.300
- People keep asking,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.647
"Why you gotta be Queer Prom?"

00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:07.286
And I say, "I'm not gonna name it

00:00:07.286 --> 00:00:08.920
"Prom That Happens to Have Tons

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.013
"of Gay People There."

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:11.179
(crowd laughing)

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:12.784
So we are centering tonight on us

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:13.617
for once, right?

00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:15.348
(crowd cheering)

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.681
(upbeat acoustic music)

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:24.208
We got a few speakers for you tonight.

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:25.940
McKenna Palmer was an intern at

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.758
the It Gets Better project.

00:00:27.758 --> 00:00:28.941
- When I was in high school, I came

00:00:28.941 --> 00:00:30.818
out my junior year, and I looked

00:00:30.818 --> 00:00:32.456
around at a school that didn't really

00:00:32.456 --> 00:00:34.453
accept LGBTQ young people.

00:00:34.453 --> 00:00:36.753
I became the president of my high school's

00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:38.244
GSA, which is the Gay-Straight Alliance,

00:00:38.244 --> 00:00:40.977
and I had so many amazing experiences

00:00:40.977 --> 00:00:42.141
in that classroom.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.280
Every week is where we could be ourselves.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.765
Where we could laugh and
talk about queer topics.

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:48.575
And what my message is to all of you

00:00:48.575 --> 00:00:52.429
is, because you're queer,
maybe you aren't normal.

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:53.262
You're different.

00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:54.095
And you know what?

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:56.457
That's not only okay, that's perfect.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:58.229
You're perfect the way you are.

00:00:58.229 --> 00:00:59.354
(crowd cheering)

00:00:59.354 --> 00:01:01.978
- We have a very special Prom Court

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:03.941
that was flown in from across the nation.

00:01:03.941 --> 00:01:05.150
Come up on the stage.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.774
(crowd cheering)

00:01:06.774 --> 00:01:07.880
We have a special guest who's

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.690
going to be anointing you King, Queen,

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.238
or Anything In-between.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.692
Can we get Adam Lambert to the stage?

00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:16.442
(crowd cheering)

00:01:18.561 --> 00:01:19.678
- Thank you.

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:21.928
Awww, you guys are so cute.

00:01:23.806 --> 00:01:26.219
You know when I was in high school,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.443
I'm gonna say it, I
graduated in the year 2000,

00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:32.157
I just said it, I said it.

00:01:32.157 --> 00:01:35.990
Life was different to
be LGBT or Q in America.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.693
It was entirely different.

00:01:38.693 --> 00:01:41.884
I think the only thing I had
was Will and Grace on TV.

00:01:41.884 --> 00:01:42.717
That was it.

00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:44.689
So it was a lot of jokes.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:46.460
Watching as an adult, over the

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.174
years, watching things change

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.633
it's been unbelievable to see how people

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:54.904
are becoming exactly who
they want to be, earlier.

00:01:54.904 --> 00:01:56.033
They're sure of it.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.012
They're able and they're
given the permission

00:01:58.012 --> 00:02:00.487
in certain places to explore.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.148
I can't believe how
fast we're progressing.

00:02:03.148 --> 00:02:05.374
And I know we have a lot of work to do,

00:02:05.374 --> 00:02:07.352
still, with equality.

00:02:07.352 --> 00:02:09.651
But man, it's really exciting to

00:02:09.651 --> 00:02:12.364
watch the growth that's happened

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.919
here in America and around the world.

00:02:13.919 --> 00:02:17.231
- This is your 2017
Buzzfeed Queer Prom Court!

00:02:17.231 --> 00:02:18.497
You might know one of the most

00:02:18.497 --> 00:02:20.546
brilliant actresses of her generation

00:02:20.546 --> 00:02:24.243
from a little show called West World.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.241
Where there's proof in the pudding,

00:02:26.241 --> 00:02:27.475
when her character finally gets to

00:02:27.475 --> 00:02:30.563
wear pants, she shoots motherfuckers up.

00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:33.919
So give it up for Buzzfeed's Queer Prom

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:35.608
Queen, Evan Rachel Wood.

00:02:35.608 --> 00:02:37.561
(crowd cheering)

00:02:37.561 --> 00:02:38.394
- Wow, this is amazing.

00:02:38.394 --> 00:02:41.706
All my dreams are coming
true in so many ways.

00:02:41.706 --> 00:02:42.815
I'm so happy.

00:02:42.815 --> 00:02:45.097
I'm happy beyond all
reason to be here tonight.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.796
And then I look at you
guys and I see progress.

00:02:47.796 --> 00:02:50.296
And it just makes me so happy

00:02:51.573 --> 00:02:52.652
to know that we can all come together

00:02:52.652 --> 00:02:55.913
on a night like this because we're family.

00:02:55.913 --> 00:02:57.881
When I'm with people in large groups

00:02:57.881 --> 00:02:59.962
like this, that I relate to so much,

00:02:59.962 --> 00:03:01.150
I hold on to that feeling.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.065
And even when you're feeling alone,

00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:05.642
remember this feeling and remember your

00:03:05.642 --> 00:03:06.969
family because we're always

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:08.993
there with you and you're never alone.

00:03:08.993 --> 00:03:10.012
Ever.

00:03:10.012 --> 00:03:11.873
I also wear a little unicorn around

00:03:11.873 --> 00:03:14.281
my neck, and it's not
just because I'm bisexual.

00:03:14.281 --> 00:03:15.747
It's because I grew up feeling

00:03:15.747 --> 00:03:18.213
like the black sheep, and

00:03:18.213 --> 00:03:19.404
feeling weird and strange

00:03:19.404 --> 00:03:20.712
and like there was
something wrong with me.

00:03:20.712 --> 00:03:21.950
And then I realized as I got older

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.157
I was not a black sheep, I was a unicorn.

00:03:24.157 --> 00:03:27.322
I was a rare, mythical creature

00:03:27.322 --> 00:03:29.887
and I was special because I was different.

00:03:29.887 --> 00:03:30.950
And I embraced that.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.762
So just remember, you're
not a black sheep,

00:03:33.762 --> 00:03:35.392
you're a unicorn.

00:03:35.392 --> 00:03:37.748
Always and forever.

00:03:37.748 --> 00:03:41.019
- We can't end a crowning ceremony

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:42.835
without a very special tradition

00:03:42.835 --> 00:03:44.993
from a very beautiful man.

00:03:44.993 --> 00:03:47.827
Can I get Daniel Franzese
on to the stage please?

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.577
(crowd cheering)

00:03:52.127 --> 00:03:53.432
- She totally goes here.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.008
(crowd cheering)

00:03:55.008 --> 00:03:56.259
I can't even tell you how beautiful

00:03:56.259 --> 00:03:57.354
it is to see all these rainbow

00:03:57.354 --> 00:04:00.724
colors in this room and all
of these rainbow people.

00:04:00.724 --> 00:04:02.447
My mom, one of her students said,

00:04:02.447 --> 00:04:04.413
"Why is a dime worth more than

00:04:04.413 --> 00:04:06.330
"a nickel if a dime is smaller

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.600
"and a nickel is bigger and heavier?"

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.767
And even though it isn't logical,

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.774
it wasn't logical that I
went to prom with a girl,

00:04:13.774 --> 00:04:15.182
and didn't really get to go with someone

00:04:15.182 --> 00:04:17.122
that I cared about, and it perhaps

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:20.988
wasn't logical that Damian in Mean Girls

00:04:20.988 --> 00:04:23.066
ended up alone at the Spring Fling.

00:04:23.066 --> 00:04:26.334
But, now I'm not the shy, closeted

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.726
queer kid at the prom.

00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:29.571
I'm here with my fiancé, Joseph.

00:04:29.571 --> 00:04:32.159
(crowd cheering)

00:04:32.159 --> 00:04:33.336
So remember even when the world isn't

00:04:33.336 --> 00:04:35.195
logical, just still be yourself

00:04:35.195 --> 00:04:38.261
and shine as bright as
the colors in our rainbow.

00:04:38.261 --> 00:04:40.559
Now they want to give me this crown,

00:04:40.559 --> 00:04:42.951
but since it's about breaking rules

00:04:42.951 --> 00:04:45.826
at the Queer Prom, I'm
just going to break this

00:04:45.826 --> 00:04:47.931
(crowd cheering)

00:04:47.931 --> 00:04:49.989
and we can all be the Queens tonight!

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.093
(crowd cheering)

00:04:51.093 --> 00:04:53.761
- Everyone here is a King, a Queen,

00:04:53.761 --> 00:04:55.947
or a Something In-between.

00:04:55.947 --> 00:04:59.697
(uplifting light rock music)

